        <obo:IAO_0000115 rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">A dystonia characterized by myoclonic jerks affecting mostly proximal muscles and dystonia, usually torticollis or writer&apos;s cramp, that typically responds to alcohol and has onset in the first of second decade of life.</obo:IAO_0000115>
        <oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">disease_ontology</oboInOwl:hasOBONamespace>
